# MySQL identifier length (64 chars)

MySQL/MariaDB limit **all** identifiers (table, column, index, foreign key) to **64 characters**.

Laravel’s default FK/index names are `{table}_{column(s)}_foreign` / `{table}_{column(s)}_index`. Long table + column names exceed 64 and fail migrate with:

`SQLSTATE[42000]: ... 1059 Identifier name '…' is too long`

## Before every migration that adds FKs or indexes

1. Compute the auto-generated name length: `strlen("{table}_{column}_foreign")` (or joined columns + `_index`).
2. If **> 64**, do **not** use `->constrained()` / anonymous `->index()` alone.
3. Use explicit short names (same pattern as `notification_template_recipient` in `2026_10_15_110000_create_email_integration_tables.php`).

```php
// ❌ BAD — auto name too long
$table->foreignId('manufacturer_model_id')->constrained()->cascadeOnDelete();
$table->index(['manufacturer_model_id', 'sort_order']);

// ✅ GOOD — explicit short names (keep under 64)
$table->foreignId('manufacturer_model_id');
$table->foreign('manufacturer_model_id', 'mm_iface_tpl_model_id_fk')
    ->references('id')->on('manufacturer_models')->cascadeOnDelete();
$table->index(['manufacturer_model_id', 'sort_order'], 'mm_iface_tpl_model_sort_idx');
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Every new FK name ≤ 64 chars
- [ ] Every new index/unique name ≤ 64 chars
- [ ] `down()` drops FKs/indexes by the **same** short name (`dropForeign('…')`, not only `dropConstrainedForeignId` when a custom name was used)
- [ ] Prefer shortening the **constraint/index** name first; only rename the table if product naming allows

SQLite (tests) is lenient; **always** check as if targeting MariaDB/MySQL production.
